Z||000008||FieroGTguy||06-10-2001||05:34 AM||||I think for anything to be "one of a kind", it shouldn't scream "poser!" with the tail lights.<P>Besides, the driver makes each car a "one of a kind", and it will take that one of a million to pay that much for a unique proudness in paying so much.  <P>Another point...  I had to sell a beautifully modified Fiero GT because I couldn't take credit for what was done.  "Yeah, I bought it like this" vs. "I did this all myself"<P>I modified a GT from bumper to bumper all by myself, and that is the kind of uniqueness that means more than money, and is a great source of pride.  You can't gain that from an auction.  You can't sign over a "bill of pride".<P>Greg||||reg||1
